From: SM-G955N Ubuntu port contributors
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: retain ENOSYS without fault dumps for native feature probes

Extend the optional-rseq diagnostic handling from patch 0006 to five known
native aarch64 feature-negotiation syscalls observed in the Ubuntu journal.
These calls still return the original sys_ni_syscall() ENOSYS. This adds no
syscall implementation and does not report success or feature equivalence.

Fallback ownership matters: glibc 2.39 handles statx (291), clone3 (435), and
faccessat2 (439) ENOSYS through generic stat, legacy clone, and legacy access
paths respectively. The close_range (436) glibc syscall wrapper does NOT
itself fall back: GLib 2.80's g_closefrom/g_fdwalk_set_cloexec callers handle
unsupported close_range with a descriptor walk. systemd 255 sd-event handles
epoll_pwait2 (441) ENOSYS with epoll_wait and caches lack of support. Other
callers can still receive ENOSYS and must handle it themselves.

Primary source references for the reviewed fallback behavior:
https://github.com/bminor/glibc/blob/release/2.39/master/sysdeps/unix/sysv/linux/statx.c
https://github.com/bminor/glibc/blob/release/2.39/master/sysdeps/unix/sysv/linux/faccessat.c
https://github.com/bminor/glibc/blob/release/2.39/master/sysdeps/unix/sysv/linux/clone-internal.c
https://github.com/GNOME/glib/blob/2.80.0/glib/glib-unix.c
https://github.com/systemd/systemd/blob/v255/src/libsystemd/sd-event/sd-event.c

Restrict the exception to native tasks: compat numbers have other meanings.
Preserve diagnostics for every other unsupported syscall, as well as actual
signal/exception/fault reporting. This classifies expected negotiation; it
is unrelated to the ABOX fault and does not make kernel logs error-free.

diff --git a/arch/arm64/kernel/traps.c b/arch/arm64/kernel/traps.c
--- a/arch/arm64/kernel/traps.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kernel/traps.c
@@ -601,6 +601,21 @@
 	 */
 	if (!is_compat_task() && regs->syscallno == 293)
 		return sys_ni_syscall();
+
+	/* These native feature probes legitimately negotiate ENOSYS on 4.4.
+	 * Keep the unsupported result; only omit the misleading register dump.
+	 * Compat syscall numbers have different meanings.
+	 */
+	if (!is_compat_task()) {
+		switch (regs->syscallno) {
+		case 291: /* statx: glibc statx_generic fallback */
+		case 435: /* clone3: glibc legacy clone fallback */
+		case 436: /* close_range: GLib caller fd-walk fallback */
+		case 439: /* faccessat2: glibc legacy access fallback */
+		case 441: /* epoll_pwait2: systemd epoll_wait fallback */
+			return sys_ni_syscall();
+		}
+	}
 
 	/* suppress magiskd ni syscall 434 reg dump in dmesg */
 	if (regs->syscallno == 434)
